TITLE:: Pscan
SUMMARY:: State recurrence over a source stream
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pwindow, Classes/Ptransduce, Classes/Pseries

DESCRIPTION::
Computes function(state, input, index, inval) for each source value and yields the new state. The first transition index is zero. Nil from the source or transition terminates without yielding nil. Length counts transitions, excluding an optional initial output. Length zero consumes no source values. State can be any object; it is not copied. Use a Function-derived initial state when mutating state. Library storage is constant, in addition to user state.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: pattern
Source, streamed with the latest inval.
ARGUMENT:: initial
Initial state evaluated once with value(inval).
ARGUMENT:: function
Transition Function receiving state, input, zero-based index and inval.
ARGUMENT:: length
Nonnegative Integer or inf, default inf. Literal, Function or Pattern sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: includeInitial
Boolean, default false. Evaluated once; yield initial state before transitions.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns the constructor arguments for archive reconstruction.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Runs the stream protocol and returns the latest inval on termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Pscan(Pseq([1, 2, 3]), 0, _ + _).asStream.all; // [1, 3, 6]
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pscan / Value stream
var values = {
Pscan(Pseq([1, 2, 3]), 0, _ + _).asStream.all; // [1, 3, 6]
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x.fold(-7,14) } { 0 }, dur: 0.18, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Musical example
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first, then evaluate this block.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \fmPiano, \degree, Pscan(Pwhite(-2, 2, 32), 0, { |s, x| (s + x).fold(-7, 7) }), \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Recaman-type recurrence
code::
Pscan(Pseries(1, 1, 16), { (n: 0, seen: Set[0]) }, { |s, x|
    var n = s[\n] - x;
    if((n < 0) or: { s[\seen].includes(n) }) { n = s[\n] + x };
    (n: n, seen: s[\seen].copy.add(n))
}).collect { |s| s[\n] }.asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pscan / Recaman-type recurrence
var values = {
Pscan(Pseries(1, 1, 16), { (n: 0, seen: Set[0]) }, { |s, x|
    var n = s[\n] - x;
    if((n < 0) or: { s[\seen].includes(n) }) { n = s[\n] + x };
    (n: n, seen: s[\seen].copy.add(n))
}).collect { |s| s[\n] }.asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x.fold(-7,14) } { 0 }, dur: 0.18, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Running average
code::
Pscan(Pseq([2, 4, 9, 1]), (sum: 0, n: 0), { |s, x|
    (sum: s[\sum] + x, n: s[\n] + 1)
}).collect { |s| s[\sum] / s[\n] }.asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pscan / Running average
var values = {
Pscan(Pseq([2, 4, 9, 1]), (sum: 0, n: 0), { |s, x|
    (sum: s[\sum] + x, n: s[\n] + 1)
}).collect { |s| s[\sum] / s[\n] }.asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x.fold(-7,14) } { 0 }, dur: 0.18, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Adaptive threshold
code::
Pscan(Pseq([0.1, 0.7, 0.9, 0.2]), (mean: 0.5), { |s, x|
    (above: x > s[\mean], mean: s[\mean] * 0.8 + (x * 0.2))
}).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pscan / Adaptive threshold
var values = {
Pscan(Pseq([0.1, 0.7, 0.9, 0.2]), (mean: 0.5), { |s, x|
    (above: x > s[\mean], mean: s[\mean] * 0.8 + (x * 0.2))
}).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: 0, cutoff: x[\mean].linexp(0,1,300,5000), amp: if(x[\above]) { 0.12 } { 0.035 }, dur: 0.25)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Numerical integration
code::
Pscan(Pseq([0, 1, 2, 1, 0]), 0, { |s, x| s + (x * 0.1) }).asStream.all;
::

State changes sweep the filter; memory and population dynamics become audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pscan / Numerical integration
var values = {
Pscan(Pseq([0, 1, 2, 1, 0]), 0, { |s, x| s + (x * 0.1) }).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: 0, cutoff: x.clip(0,1).linexp(0,1,250,6000), dur: 0.25, amp: 0.07)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Leaky integration
code::
